{%- comment -%}
  Bunnings-style "Products" menu (desktop): a single plain-text trigger
  sits in the nav row next to whatever simple links remain (Support &
  Resources etc.). Clicking it opens a grey, full-height panel sliding in
  from the left — a column of top-level categories, each with an icon,
  the label, and a chevron (same row shape as header-drawer.liquid's
  mobile flyout, so the two feel like one system).

  Reads the SAME section.blocks as itm-mega-menu.liquid — no content
  duplication:
    - `mega_item` (layout "cards" or "link") -> one row here
    - `mega_item` (layout "dropdown", e.g. Support & Resources) -> skipped,
      rendered separately by itm-mega-menu.liquid instead.

  Pass the section in: {% render 'itm-products-menu', section: section %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign accent = section.settings.mega_accent_color | default: '#e30613' -%}

{%- capture pm_chevron -%}<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%} Icon set matched by keyword against our real Teng category titles. {%- endcomment -%}
